<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a slat conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A conveyor using individual rigid slats (steel, wood, or plastic) attached to two parallel roller chains. The slats form a flat, stable platform for heavy loads such as pallets and vehicle bodies. Used in automotive assembly, appliance manufacturing, pallet handling, and any application needing a rigid conveying surface.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Slat conveyor vs. belt conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Slat conveyors use rigid slats on chains for heavy loads, heat resistance, and assembly fixturing. Belt conveyors use a flexible belt for lighter loads at lower cost. Choose slat for pallets, heavy products, and assembly lines. Choose belt for packages, parts, and general material handling.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What materials are slat conveyors made from?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Steel (carbon or stainless) for heavy loads and heat. Wood (hardwood) for pallets and finished products. Aluminum for cleanroom and lightweight applications. UHMW-PE plastic for food-grade and non-marring applications. Chain and frame are typically steel regardless of slat material.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What industries use slat conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Automotive assembly, appliance manufacturing, pallet handling, food processing, furniture manufacturing, and heavy industrial applications. Any industry needing a rigid, heavy-duty surface for large, heavy, or hot products.</p>

</div>
</div>
